  "title": "Erdős Problem #342",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "With $a_1=1$ and $a_2=2$ let $a_{n+1}$ for $n\\geq 2$ be the least integer $>a_n$ which can be expressed uniquely as $a_i+a_j$ for $i<j\\leq n$.\nWhat can be said about this sequence? Do infinitely many pairs $a,a+2$ occur? Does this sequence eventually have periodic differences? Is the density $0$?",
